what to do
Add pdf docs of UTD websites into "GDG-AskUTD\backend\data\raw_pdfs"
Each file should be named after the link of that website.

Example:

https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/support/intel-driver-support-assistant.html?updatenow&fromnotif

should be converted by removing the extra query parameters:

https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/support/intel-driver-support-assistant.html

should further be converted to 

https___www-intel-com_content_www_us_en_support_intel-driver-support-assistant-html.pdf

by replacing all colors(:) and forward slash(/) to underscore(_), 
and replacing all periods(.) to be converted to dashes(-)

your name should also contain no special characters such as ?, :, /, \, =, @, #, %, etc

You can use ctrl+p for print command to convert a website to document. You should also make sure all files from a website (if there are) are downloaded and converted to pdf with the file link as name.

Do about 40-50 pdfs each.

